# Copy to .env for local work. .env itself is gitignored.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# VITE_FIRESTORE_DB — which Firestore database this build talks to
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave it UNSET for production. The code falls back to the shop's real
# books (kinteshmobileacce) on purpose: an environment that forgets its
# configuration should land on its own data rather than on a stranger's.
#
#   production (main)                  → unset
#   test deployment / local testing    → ibellaccessory
#
# Both databases live in the same Firebase project, so the logins and the
# security rules are the same. Only the data differs.
#
# Read at BUILD time by both halves of the app — the browser bundle through
# import.meta.env, and the server through the same value inlined at build.
# One variable, deliberately: two names would be two things to set, and
# setting only one would put the browser and the server in different
# databases, which fails silently because each half works perfectly alone.
#
# Whenever this is anything but the production database, an amber strip runs
# across the top of every screen naming the database. No strip means the
# build is on the shop's real books.
#
# VITE_FIRESTORE_DB=ibellaccessory
